Given circuit is shown below. <img src="img/c4c516a8e16b2332.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,192px)"> Since the source is DC (\(\omega=0\)), the capacitor behaves as an open circuit. \[X_C=\frac{1}{\omega C}\xrightarrow[\omega\to 0]{}\infty\] The equivalent circuit is shown below. <img src="img/fc916af32e892bb3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,256px)"> Using current division, \[I_1=\frac{30}{20+10}=1~\text{A}
\tag{i}\] \[I_2=\frac{30}{8+2}=3~\text{A}
\tag{ii}\] Voltage across the capacitor, \[V_{12}=8I_2-20I_1\] Substituting (i) and (ii), \[V_{12}=8\times 3-20\times 1=4~\text{V}\] Stored energy in the capacitor is, \[E=\frac{1}{2}CV^2\] \[E=\frac{1}{2}(1\times10^{-6})(4)^2\] \[E=8\times10^{-6}\text{ J}
=8~\mu\text{J}\] Hence, \[\boxed{\text{(A)}\;8~\mu\text{J}}\]

Assume the transistor operates in the active region. Applying KVL to the collector circuit, \[12-I_{C}\times5\,\text{k}\Omega-V_{CE}=0\] Given \(V_{CE}=2\,\text{V}\), \[I_{C}=\frac{12-2}{5\times10^{3}}=2\,\text{mA}\] Using the transistor current relation, \[I_{C}=\beta I_{B}\] \[I_{B}=\frac{I_{C}}{\beta}=\frac{2\,\text{mA}}{50}=40\,\mu\text{A}\] Applying KVL to the base circuit, \[12-I_{B}R_{B}-V_{BE}=0\] \[R_{B}=\frac{12-0.7}{40\times10^{-6}}
=\frac{(12-0.7)\beta}{I_{C}}
=282.5\,\text{k}\Omega\] Since \(V_{B}=0.7\,\text{V}\) and \(V_{C}=2\,\text{V}\), \[V_{CB}=V_{C}-V_{B}=2-0.7=1.3\,\text{V}&gt;0\] Hence, the transistor is indeed in the active region and the calculated value is correct. \[\boxed{\textbf{(a) }R_{B}=283\,\text{k}\Omega}\]
